>>
Rule 1 (input tensors must have broadcastable shapes, or the second argument must be a scalar)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor ⊎ int ⊎ float} |= (ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ∀ i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i) ∨ shape(v_1, i) = 1 ∨ shape(v_2, i) = 1) ∨ ndim(v_2) = 0
>>
Rule 2 (If the input tensor v_1 is boolean, then the "other" input, v_2, must either be boolean or an integer)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor ⊎ int} |= if dtype_(v_1) = 0 then (dtype_(v_2) = 0 ∨ v_2 = 0 ∨ v_2 = 1)
